+# Tasks: Create Tar Archives (`create` command)
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/002-create-archive-command/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: [plan.md](./plan.md), [spec.md](./spec.md), [research.md](./research.md), [data-model.md](./data-model.md), [contracts/create-cli.md](./contracts/create-cli.md), [quickstart.md](./quickstart.md)
+
+**Tests**: Test tasks ARE included and are mandatory. Constitution Principle III requires every
+requirement identifier to appear in the name or docstring of at least one automated test, SC-110
+restates it, and `tests/test_traceability.py` already enforces it mechanically — the suite is
+currently `144 passed, 1 failed` because this spec's `FR-1xx`/`SR-1xx` identifiers are
+uncovered (research R-118). Tests are therefore part of the feature, not an option.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story so each story can be implemented, tested, and
+delivered independently.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies on incomplete tasks)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3)
+- Exact file paths appear in every task description
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Single project, established by `001-tarx-cli` and unchanged here (plan.md Structure Decision):
+runtime code in `src/tarx/`, tests in `tests/`, `pytest.ini` puts `src/` on `pythonpath`. There
+is no install step and no package metadata (MC-101).
+
