+## Notes
+
+- `[P]` tasks touch different files and have no dependency on an incomplete task.
+- `[Story]` labels map tasks to spec.md user stories for traceability.
+- **Every test function must carry its requirement identifiers in its name or docstring** —
+  `tests/test_traceability.py` is a gate, not a convention (constitution Principle III, SC-110).
+- **Never modify an existing test to make it pass.** MC-102 and SC-109 require the 144 inherited
+  001 tests to pass unmodified; `tests/helpers.py`, `tests/conftest.py`, and
+  `tests/test_performance.py` are extended by **addition only**.
+- `tests/test_traceability.py` is expected to fail from T001 until T037 — that is the gate working
+  as designed (research R-118).
+- No runtime module may import anything outside the standard library; the only new runtime import
+  this feature adds is `tempfile` (constitution Principle I, MC-101).
+- Resource-bound constants are **imported** from `tarx.archive`, never redefined (SR-105).
+- Commit after each task or logical group. Stop at any checkpoint to validate a story on its own.